rsary, Terry Strada slammed Saudi Arabia, whichAxios' Barak Ravidreportsis actively urging PresidentTrumpto assist them with U.S. military action.Saudi Crown Prince Mohammed bin Salman (MBS) and Trump have maintained a close relationship, while 9/11 families have expressed discomfort over U.S. officials'past engagementwith Saudi Arabia.Driving the news:\"For 25 years, administration after administration, including leaders in front of us here today, chose to protect the Saudis instead of standing with the 9/11 families,\" Strada said during the ceremony.Editor's note: This is a breaking news story and will be updated.", "published_at": "2026-09-11T13:32:40+00:00", "image_url": null, "source": {"name": "Axios", "tier": "us_major", "url": "https://www.axios.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 20, "confidence": 0.7, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 24.1, "keyword_emphasis_score": 15.0, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 12.3, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "b5afa713-541b-4315-ae59-8ba05710b765", "title": "Relative of 9/11 victim unleashes searing attack on Saudi Arabia", "url": "https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/09/relative-911-victim-unleashes-searing-attack-saudi-arabia", "summary": "A family member of one of those killed in the September 11, 2001 attacks unleashed searing criticism of Saudi Arabia live on US television during the reading of victims' names at the 9/11 Memorial Friday.The September 11, 2001 attacks were carried out by mostly Saudi hijackers orchestrated by mastermind Osama bin Laden, a wealthy Saudi who founded Al-Qaeda. Washington maintains strong military and diplomatic ties with the kingdom.", "published_at": "2026-09-11T13:30:33+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.al-monitor.com/sites/default/files/styles/social_media_share/public/2026-09/000_c7zp98m.jpg?h=69f2b9d0&itok=KBWXvfOg", "source": {"name": "Al-Monitor", "tier": "independent", "url": "https://www.al-monitor.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 50, "sensationalism": 10, "opinion_fact": 25, "factual_rigor": 50, "framing": 28, "confidence": 0.7, "rationale": {"framing": {"connotation_score": 28.0, "keyword_emphasis_score": 12.5, "omission_score": 40.0, "headline_body_divergence": 43.5, "has_cluster_context": true}}}]}}, {"article": {"id": "d67a3757-3c15-412b-9e19-01469b487581", "title": "Trump Cornered on Refusing to Release 9/11 Secrets", "url": "https://www.thedailybeast.com/trump-cornered-on-refusing-to-release-911-secrets/", "summary": "Jonathan Ernst / REUTERSPresident Donald Trump faced renewed calls to declassify 9/11 files as bereaved families honored victims on the 25th anniversary of the September 11 attacks.At Ground Zero in New York City, relatives of 9/11 victims gathered to read aloud the names of some 3,000 people who lost their lives on Sept. 11, 2001—and urged Trump, 80, to release long-awaited files about the attacks.A man who identified himself as the nephew of Lisa Marie Terry, 42, of Oakland Township, drew applause when he addressed the president.Read more at The Daily Beast.", "published_at": "2026-09-11T16:58:33+00:00", "image_url": "https://www.thedailybeast.com/resizer/v2/5FLSS3Y4LVCFRGMFXP7PUCERXE.JPG?smart=true&auth=77b96f6aa591fd84742891fce0975f7df78cd8525c9c83272df65c524302fac9&width=1200&height=630", "source": {"name": "The Daily Beast", "tier": "us_major", "url": "https://www.thedailybeast.com"}, "bias_scores": [{"political_lean": 26, "sensationalism": 12, "opinion_fact": 11, "factual_rigor": 70, "framing": 21, "confidence": 0.77, "rationale": {"lean": {"keyword_score": 54.0, "framing_shift": 0.0, "entity_shift": 1.6, "sentence_direction": 0.0, "text_score": 55.5, "source_baseline": 20, "text_shift": 5.5, "delta_max": 10, "confidence": 1.0, "top_left_keywords": [], "top_right_keywords": ["deep state"], "framing_phrases_found": [], "entity_sentiments": {"donald trump": 0.14, "t